# Configuration from Wayne Mai
wayne*
semantic_kitti/shapenet/

# --- large files: kept in the private Hugging Face dataset repo, not in git ---
# (see DATA.md; `python tools/hf_data.py pull` puts them back in place)
captures/*/scan/scan.bag
captures/*/scan/room*.ply
checkpoint/*.pth
# regenerable outputs
outputs/scannet*/
# live runs: run_live's default folder, and the per-room ones a --out_dir
# names. outputs/room07/ and room08/ are the EVALUATION csvs and stay tracked
outputs/live_session/
outputs/*_live/
# --accumulate sweeps. Regenerable from the bag and the checkpoint, both of
# which HF holds, and every number taken from them is in
# inference/document/DEMO.md -- which is the thing that has to be in git.
outputs/*_world/
# an ad-hoc sweep recorded to look at something once, under a name that
# does not match the rule above
outputs/high_wall/
custom_visual_pred/
visual_pred/
# guard.sh per-run scratch: which pid a job got, and the pause/stop flags
outputs/guard/*.state
outputs/guard/*.stop
outputs/guard/*.pause
# refine_tilt.sh / refine_height.sh keep the annotation they are about to move;
# the committed solids.json plus git history is the real undo path
captures/*/gt/solids.json.pre*
# refine_frame_pose.sh keeps the record it is about to change; git history is the undo path
captures/*/meta.json.preicp
# brainstorming specs and implementation plans: working notes for a change,
# not a description of the code. What they decide belongs in the commit
# message and in inference/document/ once it is true.
docs/superpowers/
# Thesis report planning notes: personal, not part of the code
/report.md

# Screen recordings. The GIF built from a recording is committed (it is what
# renders in the docs); the multi-megabyte source webm is not, since it can be
# re-recorded and LFS is unavailable on a fork -- see the comment in
# CleanerS_demo.webm's commit.
*.webm
!CleanerS_demo.webm
